#X text 1300 170 C-8: select 2's reject carries the page itself \, so t b b turns it into the beat row's two bangs., f 40;
#X text 2100 1420 Page 2 is the drum page: the beat row gives way \, and each row of the layout table paints one cell. A step is dim when off \, its velocity's color when on \, white for the softest to red for the loudest \, green under the playhead \, and dark past the selected track's last step. Each velocity button is its own color \, the selected pad the selected velocity's \, the other pads dimmer than any button. A bar's first step is blue \, unless it is lit \, and dark past the last step like the rest. The top row of the right 4x4 is the repeat pads \, dim purple \, the one held bright., f 60;
#X obj 2100 1000 t f f f;
#X obj 2180 1100 <= 16;
#X obj 2280 1060 r \$0-dlast;
#X obj 2350 960 t f f;
#X obj 2420 1020 * -8;
#X obj 2350 1060 +;
#X obj 2350 1110 + 135;
#X obj 2620 1020 + 127;
#X text 2100 1560 A step past the last step is dark \, lit or not: <= gives 1 inside and 0 past it \, which is the off color and gates the on one. A color of 128 or more is an RGB entry in paint's table: 128 + level - 1 at full brightness \, 136 + level - 1 at a quarter \, and 144 for a pad not selected \, dimmer than either. 145 is a bar's first step \, blue: the off color is inside x (1 + 144 x ((step - 1) mod bar == 0)) \, so 1 \, 145 or 0. 146 is a repeat pad \, 147 the one held. A step is the level c_steps sends \, 0 for off \, a velocity button its own level \, full when selected \, and the selected pad the selected level \, full., f 60;
